e":{"sanskritLocator":"7062011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"280cf1600a535c402a2df4271a4fd824fbab882a7cde2d397cb9956190979fe8","compact":"47e3076152316c3a180155512f32b78c94d3e10a673a142f895a21f67775d3de","nasal":"40ed4340752722cc65752210a1517e67d90791217a947ff9a3310cdc96f6bb4b"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-62-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":62,"verse":12,"english":"Keeping in his abode that great and redoubled which had been bestowed on Madhu by the high-souled Tryambaka, for the destruction of foes, and worshipping the same ever, Lavaņa go about and secure excellent fare( for himself) when one challenge him, desirous of reducing him (his antagonist) to ashes.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.465,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-63-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7062012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9dc598b181a859dc4bd1876cb17ddf6b4502b5c8fd153fd5732c01301d9e1a9c","compact":"38f6d094658662f99098494bfbcb79953817db74a556c74b589f75ed5f3a0577","nasal":"38f6d094658662f99098494bfbcb79953817db74a556c74b589f75ed5f3a0577"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-62-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":62,"verse":13,"english":"Beholding the city interspersed with various excellent gardens, pleasure grounds and prosperously filled with celestials and men and diverse articles of trade and merchants hailing from various countries, Satrughna, the younger brother of Bharata, attained to the satisfaction of desire and excess of delight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-70-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7062013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5efeeab2fdeb35c6aa42eba54de8b0414e83f9eb506c58477524b4e6171fe6ac","compact":"8b40eafdc1a995b346818cf56b372bee6